"Subjective
Follow up visit
Patient reports: there is improvement of symptom(s) due to energy level improved .
Patient still c/o Dull, Aching pain in left elbow area without radiation, associated with muscles soreness (scale as 70%), impaired performing ADL's with mild to moderate difficulty of holding the pot for cooking, performing household chores and mild to moderate difficulty of working long time in front of computer, long hours of driving, pushing/pulling cart, box, door.

Pain Scale: 5 /10
Pain frequency: Frequent (symptoms occur between 51% and 75% of the time)

Objective
Muscles Testing:
Tightness muscles noted along Internal oblique, External oblique
Grading Scale: Mild

Tenderness muscle noted along Internal oblique

Grading Scale: (+2) = There is mild tenderness with grimace and flinch to moderate palpation

Muscles spasm noted along External oblique, Erector spinae, Hamstrings
Frequency Grading Scale:(+2)=Occasional spontaneous spasms and easily induced spasms.

Left Elbow Muscles Strength and Joint ROM
4+/5 Flexion: 65 degree (moderate)
4+/5 Extension: 5 degree (mild)
4/5 Left side flexion: 25 degree (moderate)
4+/5 Rt side flexion: 30 degree (moderate)
4+/5 Left side rotation: 25 degree (moderate)
4/5 Right side rotation: 25 degree (moderate)

Inspection: weak muscles and dry skin without luster

tongue
thin white coat
pulse
string-taut

Assessment
The patient continues treatment for in left elbow area today.
The patient's general condition is good, compared with last treatment, the patient presents with improvement of symptom(s). The patient has decreased pain frequency, physical finding has reduced local muscles tightness and increased muscles strength. Patient tolerated treatment with increase ease with function. No adverse side effect post treatment.
Current patient still has Qi Stagnation in local meridian that cause the pain.

Plan
Today's treatment principles:
promote on moving qi to speed up the recovery, soothe the tendon.

Select Needle Size :36#x0.5" , 34#x1" ,30# x1.5"
Daily acupuncture treatment for elbow - Personal one on one contact with the patient (Total Operation Time: 60 mins)

Front Points: (30 mins) - personal one on one contact with the patient
1. Greeting patient, Review of the chart, Routine examination of the patient current condition, washing hands, setting up the clean field, selecting acupuncture needle size, selecting location, marking and cleaning the points, Initial Acupuncture needle inserted with electrical stimulation HT3, LI11, LI10

2. Explanation with patient for future treatment plan, washing hands, setting up the clean field, selecting acupuncture needle size, selecting location, marking and cleaning the points, re-insertion of additional needles with electrical stimulation LU5

Removing and properly disposing of needles

Back Points (30 mins) - personal one on one contact with the patient
3. Washing hands, setting up the clean field, selecting acupuncture needle size, selecting location, marking and cleaning the points, re-insertion of additional needles with electrical stimulation A SHI POINTS, LI12, SI8

4. Washing hands, setting up the clean field, selecting acupuncture needle size, selecting location, marking and cleaning the points, re-insertion of additional needles with electrical stimulation 

Removing and properly disposing of needles
Post treatment service and education patient about precautions at home after treatment.
Documentation
